<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Clovis I</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Clovis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Clovis I was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> in the late fifth and early sixth centuries and founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merovingian-dynasty">Merovingian dynasty</a>. He united most of the Frankish tribes, conquered much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> and converted to Catholic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>. His kingdom was the foundation on which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a> was later built.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/clovis-i.jpg" alt="Clovis I" width="185" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pethrus (talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saint_Remy_baptise_Clovis_d%C3%A9tail.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
